course: dictionary
lesson: 6140
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Milk is a word with more than one meaning. Most of the time it means the white drink from cows, goats and other animals. Context tells you which meaning you need. «Pour a glass of milk for me, please» is about a drink, because you pour it and you can drink it.
explain: Milk can also be a verb, a word for doing something. «To milk a cow or goat is to take milk from it.» The sentence explains the action for you. Some verbs are tricky, like «He milked the joke». A joke cannot give milk, so milk must mean to get as much as you can from something.
explain: Plant drinks like oat milk and coconut milk are also called milk. When you meet milk, read the words around it and ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: Milk means the white drink that comes from cows, goats and other animals.
fact: Milk is also the food that mother mammals make for their babies.
fact: To milk a cow or goat means to take the milk from it.
fact: «He milked the joke» means he got as much fun out of the joke as he could.
fact: In Britain, a «milk tooth» is a baby tooth. Children have 20 milk teeth, which fall out roughly from age 6 to 12.
exercise: «Pour a glass of milk for me, please.» What is milk in this sentence? | *The white drink from cows and goats | To take milk from a cow | To get as much as you can from something | A tooth that falls out
exercise: «He milked the joke until everyone was bored.» What does milked mean here? | To pour milk into a cup | To spill something on the floor | To take milk from a cow | *To get as much as you can from something
exercise: Which of these is a plant drink that is called milk? | A cow's bell | A milking stool | *Oat milk | A milk tooth
test: «Children have 20 milk teeth, which fall out roughly from age 6 to 12.» What is a milk tooth? | A tooth that never falls out | *A baby tooth | An adult tooth | A tooth made of milk
test: «Heat milk and a skin forms on top, which traps steam until the milk suddenly rushes over the edge of the pan.» What is milk in this sentence? | A plant drink in a carton | To take milk from a cow | *The white drink from cows and goats | To get as much as you can
exam: In «To milk a cow or goat is to take milk from it», what does the verb milk mean? | A tooth that falls out | A white drink from animals | *To take milk from an animal | A plant drink in a carton
